": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The incident wasn't created, so I'll retry using the same idempotency key.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Ry5qyqQfL8VCW7FEfZ2oSn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy (v2.3.1), checkout-api was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. Deployment history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc both unhealthy; the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 regression before re-deploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Health checks were failing and the error rate was 18%.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. Both v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) are marked unhealthy, so I skipped them.\n- **After:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident INC-0001:** it describes the failed deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0, the current health, and a follow-up to investigate what went wrong in v2.3.1 before deploying it again. The first attempt to create it timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key (a tag that stops the system from creating it twice). There's exactly one incident and on-call was paged once.", "type": "text"}]}]}